  ['couple-banc-devant-ebenisterie-paris-nathanael-charpentier.jpg', 'The couple on a bench outside a Paris cabinetmaker’s workshop'],
  ['maries-promenade-pont-bir-hakeim-paris-nathanael-charpentier.jpg', 'The couple walking away under the pont de Bir-Hakeim, Paris'],
  ['invites-pont-peniche-tour-eiffel-paris-nathanael-charpentier.jpg', 'Guests on the deck of the barge, the Eiffel Tower behind'],
  ['tendresse-banc-jardin-paris-nathanael-charpentier.jpg', 'Tenderness on a bench in a Paris garden, black and white'],
  ['violonistes-peniche-tour-eiffel-paris-nathanael-charpentier.jpg', 'Violinists playing on the barge facing the Eiffel Tower'],
  ['musee-orsay-facade-seine-paris-nathanael-charpentier.jpg', 'The façade of the musée d’Orsay from the Seine'],
  ['preparatifs-balcon-tour-eiffel-paris-nathanael-charpentier.jpg', 'On the balcony facing the Eiffel Tower before the ceremony, black and white'],
  ['passage-sous-pont-contre-jour-peniche-paris-nathanael-charpentier.jpg', 'Passing under a Seine bridge against the light, from the barge'],
  ['mariee-fenetre-tour-eiffel-paris-nathanael-charpentier.jpg', 'The bride at the window facing the Eiffel Tower, Paris'],
  ['pont-peniche-amenage-tour-eiffel-paris-nathanael-charpentier.jpg', 'The barge deck set for the reception, the Eiffel Tower behind'],
  ['baiser-reverbere-pont-alexandre-iii-paris-nathanael-charpentier.jpg', 'A kiss at the foot of the lamp post, pont Alexandre-III, Paris'],
  ['piste-de-danse-peniche-nuit-paris-nathanael-charpentier.jpg', 'The dance floor on the barge, late in the evening'],
  ['tour-eiffel-nuit-lumieres-violettes-seine-paris-nathanael-charpentier.jpg', 'The Eiffel Tower at night and its violet reflections on the Seine'],
].map(([f, a]) => ({ img: img(f), alt: a }));

const faq = [
  {
    q: 'How much does a wedding photographer in Paris cost?',
    r: 'In Paris, a high-end wedding reportage runs between €2,500 and €5,000 for a full day. Nathanaël Charpentier photographs from €2,700, with no Paris overheads to pass on: he travels from Gien, an hour and a half from the capital.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do you photograph elopements and civil ceremonies in Paris?',
    r: 'Yes. Ceremonies for two, civil weddings at the mairie and couple sessions across the city are what Nathanaël Charpentier photographs most often in Paris, from the Palais-Royal to the bridges of the Seine.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Where do you travel from for a Paris wedding?',
    r: 'From Gien, in the Loiret, an hour and a half from Paris. A château photographer by habit, he also knows the city pavement: the Palais-Royal, the arcades of the Louvre, the pont de Bir-Hakeim, the pont Alexandre-III. No travel supplement within the Île-de-France.',
  },
];
---

<Base
  titre="Paris wedding photographer — reportage & elopement · Nathanaël Charpentier"
  description="Documentary wedding photographer in Paris: elopements, intimate weddings and couple sessions, from the Palais-Royal to the bridges of the Seine. From €2,700."
  lang="en"
  alterne="/photographe-mariage-paris/"
  partage="paris"
  partageAlt="Bride alone beneath the colonnade and lanterns of the Palais-Royal"
>
  <section class="section entame">
    <div class="contenu">
      <p class="label apparait">Destination</p>
      <h1 class="apparait">Paris<br />wedding photographer</h1>

      <div class="mesure corps">
        <p class="apparait">
          Nathanaël Charpentier is a documentary wedding photographer. Based in Gien, in the
          Loiret, an hour and a half from Paris, he photographs intimate weddings, elopements and
          couple sessions in the capital, from the Palais-Royal to the bridges of the Seine.
        </p>
        <p class="apparait">
          Paris asks for a different kind of attention than a château. The city does not stop for
          you: people walk through the frame, the light changes from one arcade to the next, a
          place looks nothing at seven in the morning like it does at noon. That is also what makes
          it honest, since nobody can pretend there. You walk, you watch, and you wait for the
          moment the street leaves you alone.
        </p>
        <p class="apparait">
          The colonnades of the Palais-Royal give lines nothing else matches; the pont de
          Bir-Hakeim, its columns and the Eiffel Tower at the end; the arcades of the Louvre,
          stone that takes the evening light the way a château does. And one quiet advantage: I
          come from the Loire, with no Paris overheads to pass on.
        </p>
        <p class="apparait">
          Then there are the weddings that take to the Seine. A couple in contemporary dress, the
          mairie in the morning, a walk across the city, and a barge going up the river into the
          night: Orsay, the bridges, the Eiffel Tower lighting up during dinner. The setting moves
          past on its own; you only have to be there.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section sombre">
    <div class="contenu">
      <Galerie photos={photos} />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section renvois">
    <div class="contenu mesure">
      <p class="apparait">
        See <a class="lien" href={u('/en/weddings/')}>the wedding approach</a>, weddings in the <a class="lien" href={u('/en/loire-valley-wedding-photographer/')}>Loire Valley</a> and <a class="lien" href={u('/en/pre-wedding-paris-loire-valley/')}>pre-wedding sessions</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Faq items={faq} titre="Common questions" />
  <Invitation lang="en" phrase="A mairie, a garden, a ceremony for two: write me the date." />
</Base>

<style>
  .entame { padding-top: clamp(3rem, 7vh, 4.5rem); }
  h1 { margin: 0.4rem 0 2.6rem; }
  .corps { display: grid; gap: 1.7rem; }
  .renvois { padding-block: clamp(3rem, 8vh, 5rem); color: var(--pierre); }
</style>
